======================================================================
KEY ISSUES IDENTIFIED
======================================================================
1. jnp.gradient() uses INDEX spacing (Δξ=1) not PHYSICAL spacing
   → Need to divide by dx (in radians) then multiply by R to get physical units
   → dx = 0.052360 rad, R = 6371000 m
   → Scale factor: 1/(R*dx) = 2.997739e-06

2. No metric terms (√G) for flux-form discretization
   → Need ∂(F√G)/∂ξ / √G for proper conservative form

3. No halo exchange - gradients at face boundaries are WRONG

4. Pressure gradient in meridional direction is NON-ZERO
   → This will drive spurious meridional flow even though u2=0 initially
   → Need ∂(0.5*g*h²)/∂ξ2 = g*h*∂h/∂ξ2, which is NOT zero on the sphere!
